        "problem": "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}i{j}^{2}=$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}i{j}^{2} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}i{j}^{2}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i\\cdot {1}^{2}+i\\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+4i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}5i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}5i & =5\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+10+15 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$",
